doctype html
mixin try-it
  p(style="text-align:center")
    a.button7(href='editor.html' style="background-color:coral")
      span(style="border-right:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.5); padding-right:0.3em; margin-right:0.3em;") &#x270E;
      | Try it out
mixin clickable-face(param, name)
  -var facelink='https://paramoji.org/paramoji.svg.php?' + param
  -var editlink='editor.html?' + param
  a.onhover(href=editlink)
    img(src=facelink, alt=name)

html(lang="en")
  head
    title Paramoji
    link(rel="canonical" href="https://paramoji.org")
    link(rel='stylesheet' href='style.css')
    link(rel="icon" href="https://paramoji.org/paramoji.svg.php?v=100&a1=100&a2=100&d=50&c=0")
    meta(charset="utf-8")
    meta(property="og:image" content="https://paramoji.org/encode2.png")
    meta(property="og:image:width" content="879")
    meta(property="og:image:height" content="581")
    meta(name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1")
    meta(name="description" content="A parametric emoji that can be parameterized with five continuous dimensions. It visualizes and unifies dimensional and categorical emotional models.")
  body.page
    .twocol(style="text-align:center")
      h1.title Paramoji - A parametric emoji
    div
      h1#what-is-a-paramoji What is a paramoji?
      p
        | A paramoji is a parametric smiley face that represents facial expressions on continuous scales.
        | Unlike widespread emojis the paramojis are not defined for discretely defined states.
        | Instead, emotinal expressions are rendered
        | from five parameters that can be freely selected. They can be used to visualize manually selected, automatically detected or
        | computationally generated emotions with accuracy and with arbitrary nuances.
        | The resulting emoji style icons are expressive, exaggerated and playful. Their emotional content
        | can be easily recognized by humans.
    div(style="text-align:center")
      a(href='editor.html?v=72&a1=98&a2=36')
        img(src="encode2.png" style="max-width:500px;width:100%")
      +try-it
    h2.twocol#what-emotions-can-be-represented-with-the-paramoji What emotions can be represented with the paramoji?
    p
      | The paramoji parameterizes facial expressions with a wide variety of emotional expressions.
      | They can represent the seven
      | <a href="https://www.paulekman.com/universal-emotions">universal emotions defined by Paul Ekman</a>
      | with reasonable completeness. Here are the author's pick for those emotions. You can click the image
      | to create your own variations of those expressions.
    .ekman-table
      .table-head Normal
      .table-head Happy
      .table-head Sad
      .table-head Surpriseed
      +clickable-face('v=53&a1=35&a2=5&d=50&c=0', 'Normal')
      +clickable-face('v=100&a1=21&a2=70&d=55&c=0', 'Happy')
      +clickable-face('v=30&a1=27&a2=0&d=13&c=0', 'Sad')
      +clickable-face('v=74&a1=90&a2=94&d=0&c=0', 'Surprise')
      div(style="grid-column:1/5;height:20px")
      .table-head Fearful
      .table-head Disgusted
      .table-head Angry
      .table-head Contemptuous
      +clickable-face('v=31&a1=60&a2=40&d=0&c=0', 'Fearful')
      +clickable-face('v=0&a1=15&a2=64&d=60&c=70', 'Disgusted')
      +clickable-face('v=27&a1=56&a2=0&d=92&c=0', 'Angry')
      +clickable-face('v=60&a1=51&a2=0&d=69&c=100', 'Contemptuous')

    h2.twocol#how-can-paramojis-be-mixed How can paramojis be mixed?
    p
     | All facial expressions are generated from continuous parameters. They can
     | be interpolated into each other with arbitrary mixtures. With a slight exception in the
     | contempt dimension all graphical parameters are linearly dependent on the five input parameters.
     | This linearity ensures that the facial expressions can be smoothly interpolated into each other
     | without jumps or unintended easing.
     p(style="text-align:center")
      img(src="anim.gif" alt="paramoji animation")

    h2.twocol#paramoji-dimensions What are the five dimensions of the paramoji?
    .twocol
      p The paramoji renders from five meaningful parameters:
      ol
        li
          em Valence
          |  is the axis from bad to good, misery to pleasure, disagreement to agrement.
        li
          em Arousal
          |  is the axis from calm to aroused, inactive to active, sleepy to alarmed.
        li
          em Dominance
          |  is the axis from weakness to strength, fear to anger, submission to dominance.
        li
          em Contempt
          |  is the axis from neutral to smug, vain, disdainful and contempt.
        li
          em Control
          |  is the axis from uncontrolled to controlled, expressed to suppressed.
      p
        | With these dimensions the paramoji is able to express the emotional dimensions of the
        | <a href="https://www.researchgate.net/publication/235361517_A_Circumplex_Model_of_Affect"> Circumplex model of affect</a>
        | and the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PAD_emotional_state_model">PAD model</a>
        | of emotional states.

    h2.twocol#how-can-i-use-paramojis-on-my-website How can I use paramojis on my website?
    p
      | The easiest way to link the image directly as shown below.
      | You can set the request parameters for five paramoji dimensions from 0 to 100.
      | Optionally you can set the size parameter to get a fixed size image.
    .code
      code
        span(style="color:navy")  &lt;img src=&quot;
        span(style="color:firebrick") https://paramoji.org/<wbr/>paramoji.svg.php
        span(style="color:gray") ?
        span(style="color:firebrick") v=70
        span(style="color:gray") &amp;
        span(style="color:firebrick") a=50
        span(style="color:gray") &amp;
        span(style="color:firebrick") d=45
        span(style="color:gray") &amp;
        span(style="color:firebrick") c=0
        span(style="color:gray") &amp;
        span(style="color:firebrick") o=40
        span(style="color:navy") &quot;/&gt;

    div
      p
        | The source code is licensed as MIT and can be accessed here:
      ul
        li
          a(href='paramoji.svg.php?showSource=true') PHP code
        li
          a(href='paramoji.js') Java Script
    div
      p
        | You can use the paramoji editor to find suitable parameters.
        | To really leverage the power of paramojis these parameters must of course be dynamically derived
        | or computed.
      +try-it
    h2.twocol#references Are there any similar solutions?
    .twocol
      ul
        li
          | For a full parametric facial expression the best solution is still the
          | good old <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chernoff_face">Chernoff face</a> from the 70's.
        li
          | A lot of discrete emojis for faces and people can be found
          | on <a href="https://emojipedia.org/people/">Emojipedia</a>.
        li
          | T he <a href="https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fpsyg.2018.02396/full">EmojiGrid</a>
          | is a 2D pictorial grid of emojis for the dimensions valence and arousal.
        li
          | <a href="https://process.studio/works/aimoji-ai-generated-emoji/">AImoji</a> are AI generated emoji.
        li
          | <a href="https://www.unige.ch/cisa/research/materials-and-online-research/facsgen/home/">FACSGen</a> - A facial expression generator tool based on the facial action coding system (FACS)
        li
          | <a href="https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Parametric-face-drawings%3A-A-demographically-diverse-Day-Davidenko/07c4a0dddf6903bb80b6f445185ecc9e58e978e9">Parametric
          | Face Drawings</a> is visualization technique for facial landmarks.
        li
          | A research paper on
          | <a href="https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.206.3855&rep=rep1&type=pdf">Parametric Facial Expression Synthesis</a>.
        li
          | The <a href="https://www.researchgate.net/publication/229589717_Parametric_Generation_of_Facial_Expressions_Based_on_FACS">Facial expression generator based on FACS</a>
          | is a pay-walled paper on facial expression generation.
